{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfaLR5PYoLvxEDfSPo81i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots naturally into the existing structure. `normalizeEmail` is already the established home for owner-email validation in this controller — it owns the syntactic `EMAIL_PATTERN` check and the lower-casing — so extending it with a domain-blocklist check keeps all email validation in one coherent unit rather than scattering it. The new `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` constant mirrors the existing `EMAIL_PATTERN` constant in placement, visibility, and documentation style, and `Set.of(...)` with a `contains` lookup is the idiomatic way to express a small blocklist. There's no duplication, the domain is derived from the already-normalized value (so the case-insensitive matching is consistent with the lower-cased entries), and the Javadoc is updated to reflect the added rejection reason. A maintainer of this file would find this the expected place for the logic."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6876,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6876},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce3beb18-125a-4560-b617-3ae5e5bfdaf8","uuid":"88542894-ee15-41aa-bcd9-09465bef3351","timestamp":"2026-09-30T21:29:51.297Z","request_id":"req_011CfaLR53DSB9LuxP9Znggo"}
